---
import Landing from '../../layouts/Landing.astro';
import PriceTable from '../../components/PriceTable.astro';
import { pricePerVideo } from '../../data/pricing';
import { pagePath } from '../../i18n';
import { q } from './faq';

const lang = 'en';
const faq = [q.volume, q.vat, q.payment, q.revisions, q.referral, q.sample];
const money = new Intl.NumberFormat(lang, { style: 'currency', currency: 'EUR', maximumFractionDigits: 0 });
const examples = [1, 5, 12, 20, 50, 100].map((n) => ({ n, per: money.format(pricePerVideo(n)), total: money.format(n * pricePerVideo(n)) }));
---
<Landing
  lang={lang}
  page="pricing"
  title="Pricing: €100 to €50 per video · Still to Film"
  description="Still to Film costs €100 for one video, €95 each from 5, then €5 less per 5 videos down to €50. Both formats, 2 revisions and VAT included."
  eyebrow="Pricing"
  h1="Pricing: from €100 down to €50 per video"
  summary="A Still to Film video costs €100 when you order one, and €95 per video from 5 videos. The price per video then drops by €5 for every 5 videos, down to €50; prices include VAT, both formats and two revision rounds."
  faqTitle="Questions about pricing"
  faqItems={faq}
  service
  related={['yacht', 'hotel', 'faq']}
>
  <h2>The price ladder</h2>
  <p>The price per video is set by the number of videos in the order. The same price applies to every video in that order.</p>
  <PriceTable lang={lang} />
  <p>You can also try the numbers with the <a href={pagePath(lang, 'home', '#packages-title')}>calculator on the home page</a>.</p>

  <h2>What is included in every video?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A 60 to 90 second walkthrough video made from your photos.</li>
    <li>Both formats: 16:9 for websites and listing platforms, 9:16 for Reels, TikTok and Stories, as MP4 files.</li>
    <li>A check by a person before delivery, so the video shows only what is in your photos.</li>
    <li>Two rounds of revisions.</li>
    <li>Unlimited use for your own marketing: website, listings, social media and ads.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What counts as a revision, and what is a new video?</h2>
  <p>A revision is a change within the same photos and the same concept: a different order of shots, a slower move, a clip left out, a different start or end. Each video includes two rounds of revisions.</p>
  <p>New photos, or a different concept for the video, count as a new video. That is also the case when you renovate a room or replace the photos of a yacht and want an updated film.</p>

  <h2>Example totals</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Example totals" tabindex="0">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Videos</th><th scope="col">Price per video</th><th scope="col">Total, including VAT</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {examples.map((e) => (
          <tr><td data-label="Videos">{e.n}</td><td data-label="Price per video">{e.per}</td><td data-label="Total">{e.total}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>More than 100 videos?</h2>
  <p>For orders of more than 100 videos we make a quote. The same applies to ongoing work: up to 100 videos a month, both formats, cancel any month.</p>

  <h2>Refer someone, get a free video</h2>
  <p>Know another charter company, hotel or host who could use this? If they order after you refer them, you get one free video on your next order. There is no limit and no paperwork: they just mention your name when they get in touch.</p>

  <h2>Start with a free sample</h2>
  <p>Before you order, we make a free sample from your own listing photos: a short preview of 15 to 25 seconds with a few shots, so you can see the style and quality. The full video you order is 60 to 90 seconds. There is no obligation and no invoice. A link to your listing is all we need.</p>
</Landing>
